Docker Swarm is Docker's native container orchestration and clustering tool


Initialize a Docker Swarm on the current node
#docker swarm init

Join a swarm as a worker node
#docker swarm join --token <token> <manager_host>

Leave the Docker Swarm
#docker swarm leave

List all nodes in the swarm
#docker node ls

Create a new service in the swarm
#docker service create --name <service_name> <image_name>

List all services running in the swarm
#docker service ls

Scale a service to multiple replicas
#docker service scale <service_name>=<replica_count>

List tasks of a service
#docker service ps <service_name>

Update a running service
#docker service update <service_name>

Remove a service from the swarm
#docker service rm <service_name>

Deploy a stack using a Docker Compose file
#docker stack deploy -c <compose_file>.yml <stack_name>

List all deployed stacks
#docker stack ls

Remove a deployed stack
#docker stack rm <stack_name>
